Z||000000||PK||09-24-2001||01:55 PM||||I am sure there are other Fieros here in the UK, but no Forum for us to arrange get togethers, swap those impossible to find parts and discuss the oddities of owning a Fiero in the UK (of which there are many).<P>I am hoping to set up a UK Fiero Forum, so if you are a UK Fiero fanatic or if anyone knows of any UK owners then please send me a mail if you would be interested in something along these lines.<BR> <BR>This will not be a club as such and there will be NO FEES, SUBSCRIPTIONS or CHARGES of any kind.<BR> <BR>My apologies to the majority in the US and other countries who this may be of no relevance/interest to.<BR> <BR>Cheers<BR> <BR>PK<BR> ||||reg||3
Z||000001||Urchin||09-24-2001||02:09 PM||||I didn't realize there was much of an interest in the UK.  Good to hear.  Good luck anyhow.  If you can't get anything local going, there's always a place for you here  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/final.jpg"> <BR>If you can read this, I'm parked.||||reg||1
Z||000002||PK||09-24-2001||02:47 PM||||Thanks Urchin,<P>I'm not sure how much interest there is here in the UK either!  It is great to hear of all the events and stuff organised in the US/Canada and would be great to have something similar (but on a much smaller scale) over here.<P>Cheers<P>PK<P>p.s  nice motor<P>||||reg||1
