Z||000004||My7Fieros||09-24-2001||03:26 PM||||Why not just use this forum? See all the little flags up top? Its an international forum. This forum is actually based in The Netherlands! And there is probobly as many Canadians on here as Americans...not to mention some from other countries as well! (I didnt forget you AusFiero  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> ). Tell everyone you know in the UK to register on here! Oh yeah, welcome to the forum!<P>------------------<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><FONT COLOR="red"><B><I>My 7 Fieros</FONT></FONT></B></I>||||reg||1
Z||000005||MinnGreenGT||09-24-2001||03:43 PM||||All I can say right now is "Wish I was there!"  I hope to someday move to Scotland... get away from my busy life here.  I've been there 3 times- of course I've never seen a Fiero there, but would love to have my GT on the twisty roads (the Vauxhall Omega I rented last year was nice, but still not a Fiero).  Welcome to the Forum- and good luck recruiting!  You could also look into joining CFOG-I (Classic Fiero Owners Group - Int'l).  We've already got representation in Australia!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngtsig3.jpg">   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/halfpole.gif">  <BR>Medium Metallic Green 87 GT<BR>3.1L High Output<BR>4 Spd OD Tranny<BR>Open (read: Loud) Exhaust<BR>and More!<BR>-Rob Bartlett||||reg||1
